AB  - AI coding assistants are transforming software development, but most approaches remain code-centric and weakly connected to requirements, specifications, architectural decisions, organizational standards, and quality gates. This paper presents Spec-Driven AI, a multiagent framework for specification-centric Software Development Life Cycle (SDLC) automation. The framework combines an SDLC orchestrator, specialized lifecycle agents, human-in-the-loop gates, auditable artifact generation, and a Pattern Manager / Context Platform that provides governed context through repository indexing, document retrieval, knowledge graph extraction, adherence validation, and Model Context Protocol (MCP) tools. Spec-Driven AI treats specifications as verifiable contracts and uses agents to coordinate discovery, specification, design, planning, implementation support, testing, review, and traceability. We describe the architecture, implementation, and demonstration scenario showing how a project is registered, indexed, governed, and used to prepare structured context for SDLC agents. Screencast: https://youtu.be/w4QT-nrRgNo.
